WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.010
Part four: delegations. In a CA firm people go on leave, fall ill, or need help at the deadline. Instead of sharing a password, SimplyFile lets a person lend some of their own powers to a colleague - for one filing, one client, some clients or all clients for a year - and for set dates.

2
00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:38.804
The firm admin sees every delegation in the firm. Kavitha, a partner, is away next week, so she has already lent Anand the right to file every return of assessment year 2026-27 until she is back.

3
00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:58.501
Now Demo Partner lends Ravi, a tax preparer, the sign-off for one filing: Shree Ganesh Agarwal HUF, 2026-27. A preparer cannot sign off on his own - this lets him, for this one client and year, until the end of the month.

4
00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:08.009
Next: some clients for a year. Ravi may also mark the returns filed for Ramesh Iyer and Meera Nair this year.

5
00:01:13.296 --> 00:01:35.546
Only what Demo Partner may do himself can be lent. Ravi can now sign off the Agarwal HUF for 2026-27 - but not another client, and not another year. Everything he does through it is recorded as Ravi, for Demo Partner - so the firm always knows who did what, and for whom.

6
00:01:36.157 --> 00:01:42.177
A delegation ends by itself on its date - or can be taken back at once.

7
00:01:42.782 --> 00:01:58.742
The portal owner can delegate too: day-to-day portal work - firm approvals, portal analytics, server and sites - to a deputy, for set dates. People and access, the rule builders and setup stay with the owner alone.

8
00:01:59.344 --> 00:02:10.264
Delegations in SimplyFile: powers lent, never passwords shared - scoped, dated, recorded and revocable. Thank you for watching.
